> Though, the PIT values are nicely homogenously spread.
>
> My second approach is to look at the residuals.
> my model: M_allfish_depth_mud_DOY ("nbinomial" model with ao a spatial field)
> Fitted values: M_allfish_depth_mud_DOY$summary.fitted.values[c(1:1307),"0.5quant"]
> Only the first 1307 contain the fitted values for the observed locations (all other rows contain the fitted values for a prediction field). However when I compare fitted vs observed they don't seem to give a nice fit (see figure below). I'm I doing something wrong here (I don't apply an exponent function as what I do to the prediction field fitted values for example)?
>
> My last approach is to look at simulated data (1000x) and compare that with the observed data. That looks fine. Therefore I don't really get why my first two approaches seem to be a bit off.
>
> Cheers, Bram Parmentier
