Hi Both,
I'm still checking my model validation. Now by looking at the observed (blue in plots) versus the simulated (10x, red in plots) data. However I don't get it why those plots differ:
plot1:
SimData <- inla.posterior.sample(n = NSim, result = M_allfish, seed = inla.seed)
A_alternative <- inla.spde.make.A(mesh, cbind(totperstation$Lon_mid, totperstation$Lat_mid)) #without prediction dataframe
Am1 <- as.matrix(A_alternative)
for (i in 1:NSim){
    Betas       <- SimData[[i]]$latent[BetaRows]
    w           <- SimData[[i]]$latent[RowNum.w]
    survey      <- SimData[[i]]$latent[RowNum.Survey]
    survey      <- rep(survey, times = totperstation_test$Freq) # to assign right survey effect per sampling location
    size        <- SimData[[i]]$hyperpar[[1]]
    mu          <- exp(Betas + survey  + Am1 %*% w + log(totperstation$Dist/totperstation$Fraction)) #corrected for dist and fraction
    Ysim[,i]    <- rnbinom(n = length(mu), size= size, mu=mu)
}

plot2:
predictions <- inla.posterior.sample.eval("APredictor", SimData)
predictions <- predictions[1:1307,] #sample locations
predictions_mean <- rowMeans(exp(predictions))

I was expecting that this would give the same result.. What am I missing here?
Thanks already for your help! Bram

